<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_space",
    "A Space has a line along its bottom edge for talking. What you type there is said in the conversation the space belongs to, and pops up as a speech bubble over your character for everyone standing in the space."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_community}>{dgettext("help_space", "Saying something")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_space",
    "Type a line and press Enter, or click %{say}. In a channel's space the line goes to the channel; in a private space it goes to the other person. Either way it is in the conversation afterwards, like anything typed in the chat — and a line typed in the chat pops up over its author in the space the same way.",
    say: dgettext("chat", "Say")
  )}
  {dgettext(
    "help_space",
    "/me works there too. Every other command is typed in the chat, where its answer has somewhere to appear."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_tab_control}>{dgettext("help_space", "Typing and walking")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_space",
    "While the cursor is in the line, the arrow keys and WASD type instead of walking. Enter anywhere in the space puts the cursor in the line; Esc gives the keyboard back to the map."
  )}
</p>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_space",
    "The channel's own rules still apply: in a moderated channel only voiced people and operators are heard, and a line that is refused stays in the field with the reason under it."
  )}
</p>
